Backport picolibc upstream malloc 16-byte alignment fix to 1.8.6 (x86_64).

nano-malloc derives MALLOC_CHUNK_ALIGN from offsetof(align_chunk_t, u), and the
align_chunk_t union {void*, double, long long, size_t} has alignment 8 on x86_64
-- so malloc/calloc/realloc return only 8-byte-aligned memory. The System V AMD64
ABI requires 16 (max_align_t): code that stores SSE regs to malloc'd memory with a
16-byte-aligned store (e.g. Mesa ralloc's `movaps %xmm0,(%rax)` into an alignas(16)
struct) #GPs. Upstream picolibc fixed this by widening the alignment type to
max_align_t; adding `long double` (alignof 16 on x86_64 SysV) to the union raises
offsetof(align_chunk_t, u) to 16 with no other change. i686 is unaffected (long
double there is alignof 4) and intentionally not patched.

--- a/newlib/libc/stdlib/nano-mallocr.c
+++ b/newlib/libc/stdlib/nano-mallocr.c
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
     union {
 	void *p;
 	double d;
 	long long ll;
+	long double ld;
 	size_t s;
     } u;
